{"parentUuid":"bd7087cc-855a-4f3c-aa56-29757899afe6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Vm43PcpGWic6aWtee84yqz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UhQQNc8d4V8CrEJcDKtEcY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9361,"cache_read_input_tokens":60333,"output_tokens":104,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9361,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":104,"cache_read_input_tokens":60333,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9361},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CahQxzRgPPqo6sgR7pFyE","type":"assistant","uuid":"d675963e-4b4d-4680-96b6-e45afbdcc233","timestamp":"2026-05-04T11:01:12.366Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"705ab424-b185-46b1-96a4-0fb18926a1b1","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
{"parentUuid":"d675963e-4b4d-4680-96b6-e45afbdcc233","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2b39757b-f425-4799-921b-d831cc001a7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UhQQNc8d4V8CrEJcDKtEcY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# External Agent Plugin Protocol\n2\t\n3\t## Overview\n4\t\n5\tThe Entire CLI supports external agent plugins — standalone binaries that implement the Agent interface via a subcommand-based protocol over stdin/stdout. This allows third-party agents to integrate with the CLI without modifying the main repository.\n6\t\n7\t## Discovery\n8\t\n9\tThe CLI discovers external agents by scanning `$PATH` for executables matching the pattern `entire-agent-<name>`. For example, `entire-agent-cursor` would register as the \"cursor\" agent.\n10\t\n11\t- Binaries whose `<name>` conflicts with an already-registered built-in agent are skipped.\n12\t- Discovery runs once during CLI initialization (before building the hooks command tree).\n13\t- The binary must be executable and respond to the `info` subcommand.\n14\t\n15\t## Environment\n16\t\n17\tEvery subcommand invocation sets:\n18\t\n19\t| Variable | Description |\n20\t|---|---|\n21\t| `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` | Absolute path to the git repository root |\n22\t| `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` | Protocol version (`1`) |\n23\t\n24\tThe working directory is set to the repository root.\n25\t\n26\t## Communication Model\n27\t\n28\t- **Subcommand-based:** Each Agent interface method maps to a CLI subcommand.\n29\t- **JSON over stdin/stdout:** Structured data uses JSON. Transcripts use raw bytes.\n30\t- **Stateless:** Each invocation is independent — no persistent connection.\n31\t- **Exit codes:** `0` = success, non-zero = error. Error messages go to stderr.\n32\t\n33\t## Subcommands\n34\t\n35\t### Always Required\n36\t\n37\t#### `info`\n38\t\n39\tReturns agent metadata and declared capabilities.\n40\t\n41\t**Arguments:** None\n42\t\n43\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n44\t\n45\t```json\n46\t{\n47\t  \"protocol_version\": 1,\n48\t  \"name\": \"cursor\",\n49\t  \"type\": \"Cursor\",\n50\t  \"description\": \"Cursor - AI-powered code editor\",\n51\t  \"is_preview\": true,\n52\t  \"protected_dirs\": [\".cursor\"],\n53\t  \"hook_names\": [\"session-start\", \"session-end\", \"stop\"],\n54\t  \"capabilities\": {\n55\t    \"hooks\": true,\n56\t    \"transcript_analyzer\": true,\n57\t    \"compact_transcript\": true,\n58\t    \"transcript_preparer\": false,\n59\t    \"token_calculator\": false,\n60\t    \"text_generator\": false,\n61\t    \"hook_response_writer\": false,\n62\t    \"subagent_aware_extractor\": false\n63\t  }\n64\t}\n65\t```\n66\t\n67\tThe `capabilities` object determines which optional subcommands the CLI will call. If a capability is `false` or missing, the CLI will never invoke the corresponding subcommands.\n68\t\n69\t#### `detect`\n70\t\n71\tChecks whether the agent is present/usable in the current environment.\n72\t\n73\t**Arguments:** None\n74\t\n75\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n76\t\n77\t```json\n78\t{\"present\": true}\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\t#### `get-session-id`\n82\t\n83\tExtracts the session ID from a hook input event.\n84\t\n85\t**Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n86\t\n87\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n88\t\n89\t```json\n90\t{\"session_id\": \"abc123\"}\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\t#### `get-session-dir --repo-path <path>`\n94\t\n95\tReturns the directory where agent sessions are stored.\n96\t\n97\t**Arguments:**\n98\t- `--repo-path` — Absolute path to the repository\n99\t\n100\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n101\t\n102\t```json\n103\t{\"session_dir\": \"/path/to/sessions\"}\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\t#### `resolve-session-file --session-dir <dir> --session-id <id>`\n107\t\n108\tResolves the session file path from a session directory and ID.\n109\t\n110\t**Arguments:**\n111\t- `--session-dir` — Session directory path\n112\t- `--session-id` — Session identifier\n113\t\n114\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n115\t\n116\t```json\n117\t{\"session_file\": \"/path/to/session/file.jsonl\"}\n118\t```\n119\t\n120\t#### `read-session`\n121\t\n122\tReads session data from a hook input event.\n123\t\n124\t**Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n125\t\n126\t**Output (stdout):** JSON — [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n127\t\n128\t```json\n129\t{\n130\t  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n131\t  \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n132\t  \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n133\t  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/file.jsonl\",\n134\t  \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n135\t  \"native_data\": null,\n136\t  \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n137\t  \"new_files\": [],\n138\t  \"deleted_files\": []\n139\t}\n140\t```\n141\t\n142\t#### `write-session`\n143\t\n144\tWrites/updates session data.\n145\t\n146\t**Input (stdin):** JSON — the [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n147\t\n148\t**Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n149\t\n150\t#### `read-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n151\t\n152\tReads a transcript file and returns its raw bytes.\n153\t\n154\t**Arguments:**\n155\t- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n156\t\n157\t**Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n158\t\n159\t#### `chunk-transcript --max-size <n>`\n160\t\n161\tSplits a transcript into chunks for storage.\n162\t\n163\t**Input (stdin):** Raw transcript bytes.\n164\t\n165\t**Arguments:**\n166\t- `--max-size` — Maximum chunk size in bytes\n167\t\n168\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n169\t\n170\t```json\n171\t{\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n172\t```\n173\t\n174\t#### `reassemble-transcript`\n175\t\n176\tReassembles transcript chunks back into a full transcript.\n177\t\n178\t**Input (stdin):** JSON\n179\t\n180\t```json\n181\t{\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n182\t```\n183\t\n184\t**Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n185\t\n186\t#### `format-resume-command --session-id <id>`\n187\t\n188\tReturns the command a user can run to resume a session.\n189\t\n190\t**Arguments:**\n191\t- `--session-id` — Session identifier\n192\t\n193\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n194\t\n195\t```json\n196\t{\"command\": \"cursor --resume abc123\"}\n197\t```\n198\t\n199\t### Capability: `hooks`\n200\t\n201\tThese subcommands are required when `capabilities.hooks` is `true`.\n202\t\n203\t#### `parse-hook --hook <name>`\n204\t\n205\tParses a raw agent hook payload into a structured event.\n206\t\n207\t**Arguments:**\n208\t- `--hook` — Hook name (e.g., \"stop\", \"session-start\")\n209\t\n210\t**Input (stdin):** Raw agent hook payload bytes.\n211\t\n212\t**Output (stdout):** JSON — the parsed [Event object](#event-object), or `null` if the payload is not relevant.\n213\t\n214\t#### `install-hooks [--local-dev] [--force]`\n215\t\n216\tInstalls agent hooks for Entire integration.\n217\t\n218\t**Arguments:**\n219\t- `--local-dev` — Use local development binary path (optional)\n220\t- `--force` — Overwrite existing hooks (optional)\n221\t\n222\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n223\t\n224\t```json\n225\t{\"hooks_installed\": 3}\n226\t```\n227\t\n228\t#### `uninstall-hooks`\n229\t\n230\tRemoves installed agent hooks.\n231\t\n232\t**Arguments:** None\n233\t\n234\t**Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n235\t\n236\t#### `are-hooks-installed`\n237\t\n238\tChecks whether hooks are currently installed.\n239\t\n240\t**Arguments:** None\n241\t\n242\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n243\t\n244\t```json\n245\t{\"installed\": true}\n246\t```\n247\t\n248\t### Capability: `transcript_analyzer`\n249\t\n250\tRequired when `capabilities.transcript_analyzer` is `true`.\n251\t\n252\t#### `get-transcript-position --path <path>`\n253\t\n254\tReturns the current byte position/size of a transcript file.\n255\t\n256\t**Arguments:**\n257\t- `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n258\t\n259\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n260\t\n261\t```json\n262\t{\"position\": 12345}\n263\t```\n264\t\n265\t#### `extract-modified-files --path <path> --offset <n>`\n266\t\n267\tExtracts the list of files modified by the agent from a transcript.\n268\t\n269\t**Arguments:**\n270\t- `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n271\t- `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n272\t\n273\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n274\t\n275\t```json\n276\t{\"files\": [\"path/to/file1.go\", \"path/to/file2.go\"], \"current_position\": 12345}\n277\t```\n278\t\n279\tThe `current_position` field returns the transcript position after extraction, allowing the caller to resume from that point on subsequent calls.\n280\t\n281\t#### `extract-prompts --session-ref <path> --offset <n>`\n282\t\n283\tExtracts user prompts from a transcript.\n284\t\n285\t**Arguments:**\n286\t- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n287\t- `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n288\t\n289\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n290\t\n291\t```json\n292\t{\"prompts\": [\"first prompt text\", \"second prompt text\"]}\n293\t```\n294\t\n295\t#### `extract-summary --session-ref <path>`\n296\t\n297\tExtracts an AI-generated summary from a transcript.\n298\t\n299\t**Arguments:**\n300\t- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n301\t\n302\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n303\t\n304\t```json\n305\t{\"summary\": \"Summary text here\", \"has_summary\": true}\n306\t```\n307\t\n308\t### Capability: `transcript_preparer`\n309\t\n310\tRequired when `capabilities.transcript_preparer` is `true`.\n311\t\n312\t#### `prepare-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n313\t\n314\tPrepares/processes a transcript file (e.g., converting from raw format).\n315\t\n316\t**Arguments:**\n317\t- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n318\t\n319\t**Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n320\t\n321\t### Capability: `compact_transcript`\n322\t\n323\tRequired when `capabilities.compact_transcript` is `true`.\n324\t\n325\t#### `compact-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n326\t\n327\tBuilds a compact transcript representation for checkpoints v2.\n328\t\n329\t**Arguments:**\n330\t- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n331\t\n332\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n333\t\n334\t```json\n335\t{\n336\t  \"transcript\": \"eyJ0eXBlIjoiLi4uIn0K\",\n337\t  \"assets\": [\n338\t    {\n339\t      \"name\": \"image-1.png\",\n340\t      \"media_type\": \"image/png\",\n341\t      \"data\": \"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAA...\"\n342\t    }\n343\t  ]\n344\t}\n345\t```\n346\t\n347\tThe `transcript` field is required and must contain base64-encoded `transcript.jsonl` bytes.\n348\t\n349\tThose bytes must be the complete cumulative compact **Entire Transcript Format** JSONL for the session up to the current point in time (not a delta/scoped slice since the previous checkpoint).\n350\t\n351\tThe CLI writes these bytes byte-for-byte as the full `transcript.jsonl` file for the checkpoint, so external agents must always return the entire compact transcript accumulated so far.\n352\t\n353\tThose bytes must satisfy the checkpoints v2 format requirements:\n354\t\n355\t- UTF-8 JSONL, written byte-for-byte by the CLI to `transcript.jsonl`\n356\t- Newline-terminated JSONL: each record must end with `\\n`, including the final record\n357\t- Every line includes format metadata (`v`, `agent`, `cli_version`) alongside the entry data\n358\t- Supported top-level entry types are currently:\n359\t  - `user`\n360\t  - `assistant`\n361\t\n362\t`user` entries use `content` as an array of user blocks, typically text and optionally images:\n363\t\n364\t```json\n365\t{\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"user\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Fix the login bug\"}]}\n366\t```\n367\t\n368\t`assistant` entries use `content` as either a string or an array of assistant blocks. They may optionally include `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` fields for token usage tracking. The structured array form supports at least:\n369\t\n370\t- `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"...\"}`\n371\t- `{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\",\"input\":{...}}`\n372\t\n373\tTool output is represented inline on the preceding `tool_use` block via an optional `result` object (there is no separate top-level `user_tool_result` entry):\n374\t\n375\t- `\"result\": {\"output\":\"...\",\"status\":\"success|error\", ...}`\n376\t\n377\tExamples:\n378\t\n379\t```json\n380\t{\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"user\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Fix the login bug\"}]}\n381\t{\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:02Z\",\"id\":\"msg_123\",\"input_tokens\":150,\"output_tokens\":42,\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I updated the file.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_123\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"src/main.go\"},\"result\":{\"output\":\"package main\",\"status\":\"success\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"src/main.go\",\"numLines\":1}}}]}\n382\t```\n383\t\n384\tFor complete examples of the expected output format, see the [compact transcript test fixtures](../../cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/testdata/).\n385\t\n386\tThe compact transcript should exclude agent-native envelope/progress/system noise and retain only the normalized content needed by Entire's checkpoint readers.\n387\t\n388\tThe optional `assets` field is reserved for externalized checkpoint assets. Each asset object contains:\n389\t\n390\t| Field | Type | Description |\n391\t|---|---|---|\n392\t| `name` | string | Asset filename |\n393\t| `media_type` | string | MIME type for the asset |\n394\t| `data` | string | Base64-encoded asset bytes |\n395\t\n396\tCurrent CLI behavior:\n397\t- If `compact_transcript` is missing or `false`, the CLI will skip compact transcript generation for that external agent, fall back to raw transcript storage, and log a warning.\n398\t- If `compact-transcript` fails or returns invalid output, the CLI will also fall back to raw transcript storage and log a warning.\n399\t- The CLI normalizes `transcript` bytes by appending a trailing newline when missing, and treats whitespace-only transcript output as invalid.\n400\t- If `assets` are returned, the CLI accepts them in the protocol shape but currently ignores them for storage and read paths.\n401\t\n402\t### Capability: `token_calculator`\n403\t\n404\tRequired when `capabilities.token_calculator` is `true`.\n405\t\n406\t#### `calculate-tokens --offset <n>`\n407\t\n408\tCalculates token usage from a transcript.\n409\t\n410\t**Input (stdin):** Raw transcript bytes.\n411\t\n412\t**Arguments:**\n413\t- `--offset` — Byte offset to start calculating from\n414\t\n415\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n416\t\n417\t```json\n418\t{\n419\t  \"input_tokens\": 1500,\n420\t  \"cache_creation_tokens\": 0,\n421\t  \"cache_read_tokens\": 200,\n422\t  \"output_tokens\": 500,\n423\t  \"api_call_count\": 3,\n424\t  \"subagent_tokens\": null\n425\t}\n426\t```\n427\t\n428\tOnly `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` are required. The optional fields (`cache_creation_tokens`, `cache_read_tokens`, `api_call_count`) default to `0` if omitted. `subagent_tokens` is an optional nested object with the same structure, for agents that spawn subagents.\n429\t\n430\t### Capability: `text_generator`\n431\t\n432\tRequired when `capabilities.text_generator` is `true`.\n433\t\n434\tExternal agents that declare `capabilities.text_generator: true` can be used as\n435\tsummary providers for `entire explain --generate` and checkpoint auto-summarize.\n436\tConfigure them with:\n437\t\n438\t```bash\n439\tentire configure --summarize-provider <agent-name> [--summarize-model <model>]\n440\t```\n441\t\n442\tThe provider name is derived from the executable name `entire-agent-<agent-name>`.\n443\tThe CLI passes Entire's summary prompt on stdin to `generate-text --model <model>`\n444\tand expects `{\"text\":\"...\"}` on stdout.\n445\t\n446\t#### `generate-text --model <model>`\n447\t\n448\tGenerates text using the agent's underlying LLM.\n449\t\n450\t**Input (stdin):** Prompt text.\n451\t\n452\t**Arguments:**\n453\t- `--model` — Model to use for generation\n454\t\n455\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n456\t\n457\t```json\n458\t{\"text\": \"Generated response text\"}\n459\t```\n460\t\n461\t### Capability: `hook_response_writer`\n462\t\n463\tRequired when `capabilities.hook_response_writer` is `true`.\n464\t\n465\t#### `write-hook-response --message <message>`\n466\t\n467\tWrites a message in the agent's native hook response format.\n468\t\n469\t**Arguments:**\n470\t- `--message` — Message to write\n471\t\n472\t**Output (stdout):** Agent-native format bytes (e.g., JSONL for Claude Code).\n473\t\n474\t### Capability: `subagent_aware_extractor`\n475\t\n476\tRequired when `capabilities.subagent_aware_extractor` is `true`.\n477\t\n478\t#### `extract-all-modified-files --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n479\t\n480\tExtracts modified files from both the main transcript and any subagent transcripts.\n481\t\n482\t**Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n483\t\n484\t**Arguments:**\n485\t- `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n486\t- `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n487\t\n488\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n489\t\n490\t```json\n491\t{\"files\": [\"file1.go\", \"file2.go\"]}\n492\t```\n493\t\n494\t#### `calculate-total-tokens --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n495\t\n496\tCalculates total token usage across main transcript and subagent transcripts.\n497\t\n498\t**Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n499\t\n500\t**Arguments:**\n501\t- `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n502\t- `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n503\t\n504\t**Output (stdout):** JSON\n505\t\n506\t```json\n507\t{\n508\t  \"input_tokens\": 5000,\n509\t  \"cache_creation_tokens\": 0,\n510\t  \"cache_read_tokens\": 1000,\n511\t  \"output_tokens\": 2000,\n512\t  \"api_call_count\": 8,\n513\t  \"subagent_tokens\": {\n514\t    \"input_tokens\": 2000,\n515\t    \"output_tokens\": 800\n516\t  }\n517\t}\n518\t```\n519\t\n520\tSame token usage format as `calculate-tokens`. The `subagent_tokens` field aggregates usage from all subagents.\n521\t\n522\t## Shared Object Definitions\n523\t\n524\t### HookInput Object\n525\t\n526\tThe HookInput object is passed via stdin to `get-session-id` and `read-session`.\n527\t\n528\t```json\n529\t{\n530\t  \"hook_type\": \"stop\",\n531\t  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n532\t  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n533\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n534\t  \"user_prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n535\t  \"tool_name\": \"Write\",\n536\t  \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_abc123\",\n537\t  \"tool_input\": {\"path\": \"/src/main.go\"},\n538\t  \"raw_data\": {\"custom_field\": \"value\"}\n539\t}\n540\t```\n541\t\n542\t| Field | Type | Description |\n543\t|---|---|---|\n544\t| `hook_type` | string | Hook type: `session_start`, `session_end`, `user_prompt_submit`, `stop`, `pre_tool_use`, `post_tool_use` |\n545\t| `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n546\t| `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific session reference (typically a file path) |\n547\t| `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp |\n548\t| `user_prompt` | string | User's prompt text (from `user_prompt_submit` hooks). Optional. |\n549\t| `tool_name` | string | Tool name (from `pre_tool_use`/`post_tool_use` hooks). Optional. |\n550\t| `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID. Optional. |\n551\t| `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON. Optional. |\n552\t| `raw_data` | object | Agent-specific data for extension. Optional. |\n553\t\n554\t### AgentSession Object\n555\t\n556\tUsed as input to `write-session` and output from `read-session`.\n557\t\n558\t```json\n559\t{\n560\t  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n561\t  \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n562\t  \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n563\t  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n564\t  \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n565\t  \"native_data\": null,\n566\t  \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n567\t  \"new_files\": [\"src/new_file.go\"],\n568\t  \"deleted_files\": []\n569\t}\n570\t```\n571\t\n572\t| Field | Type | Description |\n573\t|---|---|---|\n574\t| `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n575\t| `agent_name` | string | Agent registry name |\n576\t| `repo_path` | string | Absolute path to the repository |\n577\t| `session_ref` | string | Path/reference to session in agent's storage |\n578\t| `start_time` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp of session start |\n579\t| `native_data` | bytes/null | Session content in agent's native format (opaque to CLI) |\n580\t| `modified_files` | string[] | Files modified during the session |\n581\t| `new_files` | string[] | Files created during the session |\n582\t| `deleted_files` | string[] | Files deleted during the session |\n583\t\n584\t### Event Object\n585\t\n586\tReturned by `parse-hook`. Represents a normalized lifecycle event.\n587\t\n588\t```json\n589\t{\n590\t  \"type\": 3,\n591\t  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n592\t  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n593\t  \"prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n594\t  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\",\n595\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\"\n596\t}\n597\t```\n598\t\n599\t| Field | Type | Description |\n600\t|---|---|---|\n601\t| `type` | int | **Required.** Event type (see table below) |\n602\t| `session_id` | string | **Required.** Agent session identifier |\n603\t| `previous_session_id` | string | Non-empty when this event represents a session continuation/handoff. Optional. |\n604\t| `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific transcript reference. Optional. |\n605\t| `prompt` | string | User's prompt text (on `TurnStart` events). Optional. |\n606\t| `model` | string | LLM model identifier. Optional. |\n607\t| `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp. Optional. |\n608\t| `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n609\t| `subagent_id` | string | Subagent instance ID (for `SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n610\t| `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON (for subagent type/description extraction). Optional. |\n611\t| `subagent_type` | string | Kind of subagent (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n612\t| `task_description` | string | Subagent task description. Optional. |\n613\t| `response_message` | string | Message to display to the user via the agent. Optional. |\n614\t| `metadata` | object | Agent-specific state preserved across events. Optional. |\n615\t\n616\t**Event types:**\n617\t\n618\t| Value | Name | Description |\n619\t|---|---|---|\n620\t| 1 | SessionStart | Agent session has begun |\n621\t| 2 | TurnStart | User submitted a prompt, agent is about to work |\n622\t| 3 | TurnEnd | Agent finished responding to a prompt |\n623\t| 4 | Compaction | Agent is compressing its context window (triggers save + offset reset) |\n624\t| 5 | SessionEnd | Session has been terminated |\n625\t| 6 | SubagentStart | A subagent (task) has been spawned |\n626\t| 7 | SubagentEnd | A subagent (task) has completed |\n627\t\n628\t## Error Handling\n629\t\n630\t- Exit code `0` indicates success.\n631\t- Any non-zero exit code indicates an error.\n632\t- Error messages should be written to stderr.\n633\t- The CLI captures stderr and wraps it in a Go error.\n634\t- If the binary is not found in PATH, the agent is simply not registered.\n635\t- If `info` fails or returns invalid JSON, the binary is skipped during discovery.\n636\t\n637\t## Versioning\n638\t\n639\tThe protocol version is declared in the `info` response (`protocol_version` field) and set via `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` environment variable. The CLI checks that the binary's protocol version matches its expected version before registering the agent.\n640\t\n641\tFuture protocol versions may add new subcommands or capabilities. Existing subcommands will maintain backwards compatibility within a major version.\n642\t"}]},"uuid":"903bf94e-6508-42a7-a7b3-3938eae422ac","timestamp":"2026-05-04T11:01:12.374Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md","content":"# External Agent Plugin Protocol\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Entire CLI supports external agent plugins — standalone binaries that implement the Agent interface via a subcommand-based protocol over stdin/stdout. This allows third-party agents to integrate with the CLI without modifying the main repository.\n\n## Discovery\n\nThe CLI discovers external agents by scanning `$PATH` for executables matching the pattern `entire-agent-<name>`. For example, `entire-agent-cursor` would register as the \"cursor\" agent.\n\n- Binaries whose `<name>` conflicts with an already-registered built-in agent are skipped.\n- Discovery runs once during CLI initialization (before building the hooks command tree).\n- The binary must be executable and respond to the `info` subcommand.\n\n## Environment\n\nEvery subcommand invocation sets:\n\n| Variable | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` | Absolute path to the git repository root |\n| `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` | Protocol version (`1`) |\n\nThe working directory is set to the repository root.\n\n## Communication Model\n\n- **Subcommand-based:** Each Agent interface method maps to a CLI subcommand.\n- **JSON over stdin/stdout:** Structured data uses JSON. Transcripts use raw bytes.\n- **Stateless:** Each invocation is independent — no persistent connection.\n- **Exit codes:** `0` = success, non-zero = error. Error messages go to stderr.\n\n## Subcommands\n\n### Always Required\n\n#### `info`\n\nReturns agent metadata and declared capabilities.\n\n**Arguments:** None\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\n  \"protocol_version\": 1,\n  \"name\": \"cursor\",\n  \"type\": \"Cursor\",\n  \"description\": \"Cursor - AI-powered code editor\",\n  \"is_preview\": true,\n  \"protected_dirs\": [\".cursor\"],\n  \"hook_names\": [\"session-start\", \"session-end\", \"stop\"],\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"hooks\": true,\n    \"transcript_analyzer\": true,\n    \"compact_transcript\": true,\n    \"transcript_preparer\": false,\n    \"token_calculator\": false,\n    \"text_generator\": false,\n    \"hook_response_writer\": false,\n    \"subagent_aware_extractor\": false\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `capabilities` object determines which optional subcommands the CLI will call. If a capability is `false` or missing, the CLI will never invoke the corresponding subcommands.\n\n#### `detect`\n\nChecks whether the agent is present/usable in the current environment.\n\n**Arguments:** None\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"present\": true}\n```\n\n#### `get-session-id`\n\nExtracts the session ID from a hook input event.\n\n**Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"session_id\": \"abc123\"}\n```\n\n#### `get-session-dir --repo-path <path>`\n\nReturns the directory where agent sessions are stored.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--repo-path` — Absolute path to the repository\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"session_dir\": \"/path/to/sessions\"}\n```\n\n#### `resolve-session-file --session-dir <dir> --session-id <id>`\n\nResolves the session file path from a session directory and ID.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--session-dir` — Session directory path\n- `--session-id` — Session identifier\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"session_file\": \"/path/to/session/file.jsonl\"}\n```\n\n#### `read-session`\n\nReads session data from a hook input event.\n\n**Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON — [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n  \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n  \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/file.jsonl\",\n  \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"native_data\": null,\n  \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n  \"new_files\": [],\n  \"deleted_files\": []\n}\n```\n\n#### `write-session`\n\nWrites/updates session data.\n\n**Input (stdin):** JSON — the [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n\n**Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n\n#### `read-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n\nReads a transcript file and returns its raw bytes.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n\n**Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n\n#### `chunk-transcript --max-size <n>`\n\nSplits a transcript into chunks for storage.\n\n**Input (stdin):** Raw transcript bytes.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--max-size` — Maximum chunk size in bytes\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n```\n\n#### `reassemble-transcript`\n\nReassembles transcript chunks back into a full transcript.\n\n**Input (stdin):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n```\n\n**Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n\n#### `format-resume-command --session-id <id>`\n\nReturns the command a user can run to resume a session.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--session-id` — Session identifier\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"command\": \"cursor --resume abc123\"}\n```\n\n### Capability: `hooks`\n\nThese subcommands are required when `capabilities.hooks` is `true`.\n\n#### `parse-hook --hook <name>`\n\nParses a raw agent hook payload into a structured event.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--hook` — Hook name (e.g., \"stop\", \"session-start\")\n\n**Input (stdin):** Raw agent hook payload bytes.\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON — the parsed [Event object](#event-object), or `null` if the payload is not relevant.\n\n#### `install-hooks [--local-dev] [--force]`\n\nInstalls agent hooks for Entire integration.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--local-dev` — Use local development binary path (optional)\n- `--force` — Overwrite existing hooks (optional)\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"hooks_installed\": 3}\n```\n\n#### `uninstall-hooks`\n\nRemoves installed agent hooks.\n\n**Arguments:** None\n\n**Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n\n#### `are-hooks-installed`\n\nChecks whether hooks are currently installed.\n\n**Arguments:** None\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"installed\": true}\n```\n\n### Capability: `transcript_analyzer`\n\nRequired when `capabilities.transcript_analyzer` is `true`.\n\n#### `get-transcript-position --path <path>`\n\nReturns the current byte position/size of a transcript file.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"position\": 12345}\n```\n\n#### `extract-modified-files --path <path> --offset <n>`\n\nExtracts the list of files modified by the agent from a transcript.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n- `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"path/to/file1.go\", \"path/to/file2.go\"], \"current_position\": 12345}\n```\n\nThe `current_position` field returns the transcript position after extraction, allowing the caller to resume from that point on subsequent calls.\n\n#### `extract-prompts --session-ref <path> --offset <n>`\n\nExtracts user prompts from a transcript.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n- `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"prompts\": [\"first prompt text\", \"second prompt text\"]}\n```\n\n#### `extract-summary --session-ref <path>`\n\nExtracts an AI-generated summary from a transcript.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"summary\": \"Summary text here\", \"has_summary\": true}\n```\n\n### Capability: `transcript_preparer`\n\nRequired when `capabilities.transcript_preparer` is `true`.\n\n#### `prepare-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n\nPrepares/processes a transcript file (e.g., converting from raw format).\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n\n**Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n\n### Capability: `compact_transcript`\n\nRequired when `capabilities.compact_transcript` is `true`.\n\n#### `compact-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n\nBuilds a compact transcript representation for checkpoints v2.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\n  \"transcript\": \"eyJ0eXBlIjoiLi4uIn0K\",\n  \"assets\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"image-1.png\",\n      \"media_type\": \"image/png\",\n      \"data\": \"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAA...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe `transcript` field is required and must contain base64-encoded `transcript.jsonl` bytes.\n\nThose bytes must be the complete cumulative compact **Entire Transcript Format** JSONL for the session up to the current point in time (not a delta/scoped slice since the previous checkpoint).\n\nThe CLI writes these bytes byte-for-byte as the full `transcript.jsonl` file for the checkpoint, so external agents must always return the entire compact transcript accumulated so far.\n\nThose bytes must satisfy the checkpoints v2 format requirements:\n\n- UTF-8 JSONL, written byte-for-byte by the CLI to `transcript.jsonl`\n- Newline-terminated JSONL: each record must end with `\\n`, including the final record\n- Every line includes format metadata (`v`, `agent`, `cli_version`) alongside the entry data\n- Supported top-level entry types are currently:\n  - `user`\n  - `assistant`\n\n`user` entries use `content` as an array of user blocks, typically text and optionally images:\n\n```json\n{\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"user\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Fix the login bug\"}]}\n```\n\n`assistant` entries use `content` as either a string or an array of assistant blocks. They may optionally include `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` fields for token usage tracking. The structured array form supports at least:\n\n- `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"...\"}`\n- `{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\",\"input\":{...}}`\n\nTool output is represented inline on the preceding `tool_use` block via an optional `result` object (there is no separate top-level `user_tool_result` entry):\n\n- `\"result\": {\"output\":\"...\",\"status\":\"success|error\", ...}`\n\nExamples:\n\n```json\n{\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"user\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Fix the login bug\"}]}\n{\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:02Z\",\"id\":\"msg_123\",\"input_tokens\":150,\"output_tokens\":42,\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I updated the file.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_123\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"src/main.go\"},\"result\":{\"output\":\"package main\",\"status\":\"success\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"src/main.go\",\"numLines\":1}}}]}\n```\n\nFor complete examples of the expected output format, see the [compact transcript test fixtures](../../cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/testdata/).\n\nThe compact transcript should exclude agent-native envelope/progress/system noise and retain only the normalized content needed by Entire's checkpoint readers.\n\nThe optional `assets` field is reserved for externalized checkpoint assets. Each asset object contains:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `name` | string | Asset filename |\n| `media_type` | string | MIME type for the asset |\n| `data` | string | Base64-encoded asset bytes |\n\nCurrent CLI behavior:\n- If `compact_transcript` is missing or `false`, the CLI will skip compact transcript generation for that external agent, fall back to raw transcript storage, and log a warning.\n- If `compact-transcript` fails or returns invalid output, the CLI will also fall back to raw transcript storage and log a warning.\n- The CLI normalizes `transcript` bytes by appending a trailing newline when missing, and treats whitespace-only transcript output as invalid.\n- If `assets` are returned, the CLI accepts them in the protocol shape but currently ignores them for storage and read paths.\n\n### Capability: `token_calculator`\n\nRequired when `capabilities.token_calculator` is `true`.\n\n#### `calculate-tokens --offset <n>`\n\nCalculates token usage from a transcript.\n\n**Input (stdin):** Raw transcript bytes.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--offset` — Byte offset to start calculating from\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\n  \"input_tokens\": 1500,\n  \"cache_creation_tokens\": 0,\n  \"cache_read_tokens\": 200,\n  \"output_tokens\": 500,\n  \"api_call_count\": 3,\n  \"subagent_tokens\": null\n}\n```\n\nOnly `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` are required. The optional fields (`cache_creation_tokens`, `cache_read_tokens`, `api_call_count`) default to `0` if omitted. `subagent_tokens` is an optional nested object with the same structure, for agents that spawn subagents.\n\n### Capability: `text_generator`\n\nRequired when `capabilities.text_generator` is `true`.\n\nExternal agents that declare `capabilities.text_generator: true` can be used as\nsummary providers for `entire explain --generate` and checkpoint auto-summarize.\nConfigure them with:\n\n```bash\nentire configure --summarize-provider <agent-name> [--summarize-model <model>]\n```\n\nThe provider name is derived from the executable name `entire-agent-<agent-name>`.\nThe CLI passes Entire's summary prompt on stdin to `generate-text --model <model>`\nand expects `{\"text\":\"...\"}` on stdout.\n\n#### `generate-text --model <model>`\n\nGenerates text using the agent's underlying LLM.\n\n**Input (stdin):** Prompt text.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--model` — Model to use for generation\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"text\": \"Generated response text\"}\n```\n\n### Capability: `hook_response_writer`\n\nRequired when `capabilities.hook_response_writer` is `true`.\n\n#### `write-hook-response --message <message>`\n\nWrites a message in the agent's native hook response format.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--message` — Message to write\n\n**Output (stdout):** Agent-native format bytes (e.g., JSONL for Claude Code).\n\n### Capability: `subagent_aware_extractor`\n\nRequired when `capabilities.subagent_aware_extractor` is `true`.\n\n#### `extract-all-modified-files --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n\nExtracts modified files from both the main transcript and any subagent transcripts.\n\n**Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n- `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"file1.go\", \"file2.go\"]}\n```\n\n#### `calculate-total-tokens --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n\nCalculates total token usage across main transcript and subagent transcripts.\n\n**Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n- `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n\n**Output (stdout):** JSON\n\n```json\n{\n  \"input_tokens\": 5000,\n  \"cache_creation_tokens\": 0,\n  \"cache_read_tokens\": 1000,\n  \"output_tokens\": 2000,\n  \"api_call_count\": 8,\n  \"subagent_tokens\": {\n    \"input_tokens\": 2000,\n    \"output_tokens\": 800\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSame token usage format as `calculate-tokens`. The `subagent_tokens` field aggregates usage from all subagents.\n\n## Shared Object Definitions\n\n### HookInput Object\n\nThe HookInput object is passed via stdin to `get-session-id` and `read-session`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hook_type\": \"stop\",\n  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"user_prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n  \"tool_name\": \"Write\",\n  \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_abc123\",\n  \"tool_input\": {\"path\": \"/src/main.go\"},\n  \"raw_data\": {\"custom_field\": \"value\"}\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `hook_type` | string | Hook type: `session_start`, `session_end`, `user_prompt_submit`, `stop`, `pre_tool_use`, `post_tool_use` |\n| `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n| `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific session reference (typically a file path) |\n| `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp |\n| `user_prompt` | string | User's prompt text (from `user_prompt_submit` hooks). Optional. |\n| `tool_name` | string | Tool name (from `pre_tool_use`/`post_tool_use` hooks). Optional. |\n| `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID. Optional. |\n| `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON. Optional. |\n| `raw_data` | object | Agent-specific data for extension. Optional. |\n\n### AgentSession Object\n\nUsed as input to `write-session` and output from `read-session`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n  \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n  \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n  \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"native_data\": null,\n  \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n  \"new_files\": [\"src/new_file.go\"],\n  \"deleted_files\": []\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n| `agent_name` | string | Agent registry name |\n| `repo_path` | string | Absolute path to the repository |\n| `session_ref` | string | Path/reference to session in agent's storage |\n| `start_time` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp of session start |\n| `native_data` | bytes/null | Session content in agent's native format (opaque to CLI) |\n| `modified_files` | string[] | Files modified during the session |\n| `new_files` | string[] | Files created during the session |\n| `deleted_files` | string[] | Files deleted during the session |\n\n### Event Object\n\nReturned by `parse-hook`. Represents a normalized lifecycle event.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": 3,\n  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n  \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `type` | int | **Required.** Event type (see table below) |\n| `session_id` | string | **Required.** Agent session identifier |\n| `previous_session_id` | string | Non-empty when this event represents a session continuation/handoff. Optional. |\n| `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific transcript reference. Optional. |\n| `prompt` | string | User's prompt text (on `TurnStart` events). Optional. |\n| `model` | string | LLM model identifier. Optional. |\n| `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp. Optional. |\n| `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n| `subagent_id` | string | Subagent instance ID (for `SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n| `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON (for subagent type/description extraction). Optional. |\n| `subagent_type` | string | Kind of subagent (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n| `task_description` | string | Subagent task description. Optional. |\n| `response_message` | string | Message to display to the user via the agent. Optional. |\n| `metadata` | object | Agent-specific state preserved across events. Optional. |\n\n**Event types:**\n\n| Value | Name | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | SessionStart | Agent session has begun |\n| 2 | TurnStart | User submitted a prompt, agent is about to work |\n| 3 | TurnEnd | Agent finished responding to a prompt |\n| 4 | Compaction | Agent is compressing its context window (triggers save + offset reset) |\n| 5 | SessionEnd | Session has been terminated |\n| 6 | SubagentStart | A subagent (task) has been spawned |\n| 7 | SubagentEnd | A subagent (task) has completed |\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- Exit code `0` indicates success.\n- Any non-zero exit code indicates an error.\n- Error messages should be written to stderr.\n- The CLI captures stderr and wraps it in a Go error.\n- If the binary is not found in PATH, the agent is simply not registered.\n- If `info` fails or returns invalid JSON, the binary is skipped during discovery.\n\n## Versioning\n\nThe protocol version is declared in the `info` response (`protocol_version` field) and set via `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` environment variable. The CLI checks that the binary's protocol version matches its expected version before registering the agent.\n\nFuture protocol versions may add new subcommands or capabilities. Existing subcommands will maintain backwards compatibility within a major version.\n","numLines":642,"startLine":1,"totalLines":642}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d675963e-4b4d-4680-96b6-e45afbdcc233","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"705ab424-b185-46b1-96a4-0fb18926a1b1","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
