{"parentUuid":"1d21392c-8cd0-4bd5-bdb6-8c2226992167","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TWDQpXYUUppMyp2RVbJoVx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the picture. Two things to call out:\n\n**This is a different mechanism than external agents.** The existing system (`entire-agent-<name>` binaries) implements a 15+ subcommand JSON protocol (`info`, `detect`, `parse-hook`, `compact-transcript`, …) discovered in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go:69`. That's not what you want for `entire-pgr`.\n\nWhat you're describing is **git-style command extension**: `entire pgr <args>` → `exec(\"entire-pgr\", args...)` with stdin/stdout/stderr/exit-code passthrough, no protocol. Like `git foo` → `git-foo`, `kubectl foo` → `kubectl-foo`.\n\nWhat's needed:\n\n1. **Separate prefix and discovery** — keep `entire-agent-*` reserved for the protocol, use `entire-*` (excluding `entire-agent-*`) for passthrough plugins. Otherwise the agent discovery will try to call `entire-pgr info` and skip it when JSON parsing fails.\n2. **Lazy resolution in root command** — Cobra errors on unknown subcommands by default. Either intercept args in `main.go` before `root.Execute()`, or set the root's `RunE`/`Args` to dispatch unknown first-arg → `exec.LookPath(\"entire-\" + arg)`. Built-ins must win on collision.\n3. **Disable flag parsing on the dispatch path** — so `entire pgr --foo` passes `--foo` through verbatim instead of Cobra rejecting it. `DisableFlagParsing: true` + `Args: cobra.ArbitraryArgs` is the usual recipe.\n4. **Pass-through env/cwd** — likely set `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT`/cwd consistent with existing `external.Agent.run` (`external.go:438`) so `entire-pgr` sees the same context.\n5. **Help/listing (optional)** — git scans `PATH` once for `git help -a`. You can skip this initially and add an eager scan later if `entire help` should list discovered plugins.\n\nThe main tradeoff is **lazy vs. eager discovery**. Lazy = zero startup cost, only resolves on use, but `entire help` won't list `pgr`. Eager = nicer help, costs a PATH scan on every invocation. Recommend starting lazy + adding a help integration later.\n\nWant me to draft the dispatcher? Roughly ~50 lines in `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` plus a discovery-skip rule in `agent/external/discovery.go` to ignore non-`agent-` prefixed binaries."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4224,"cache_read_input_tokens":87505,"output_tokens":2576,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4224,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2576,"cache_read_input_tokens":87505,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4224},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CahR1kqxBhnQUnAk5B4nN","type":"assistant","uuid":"c154c8f4-31d5-4b93-82a4-389f9844c8a4","timestamp":"2026-05-04T11:02:29.772Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"705ab424-b185-46b1-96a4-0fb18926a1b1","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
