{"parentUuid":"79b2a55d-e9ff-4caf-8350-4c155b42d624","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_018ah3JDrTVTTYHNcjm2o1MX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's how the three differ:\n\n**git** — pure PATH-scan, lazy\n- No registry, no manifest. When you type `git foo` and `foo` isn't built-in, git execvp's `git-foo` from PATH with the remaining args. That's it.\n- `git help -a` does an on-demand PATH walk to list `git-*` binaries, but normal invocation doesn't.\n- Process replacement via `execvp`, so signals/TTY just work.\n\n**kubectl** — PATH-scan, lazy with explicit listing\n- Same model as git: `kubectl foo` → `kubectl-foo` on PATH, exec'd with remaining args. Hyphens in the plugin name map to underscores in the binary (`kubectl foo-bar` → `kubectl-foo_bar`).\n- Adds `kubectl plugin list` that walks PATH and reports conflicts/shadowing (built-ins always win, with a warning).\n- Uses `os/exec`, not exec replacement.\n\n**gh** — managed install dir, eager Cobra registration (`pkg/cmd/extension/`, `pkg/cmd/root/extension.go`, `pkg/cmd/root/root.go:191-203`)\n- **Doesn't scan PATH at all.** Extensions live in `~/.local/share/gh/extensions/<gh-name>/` — a directory gh manages itself via `gh extension install/list/upgrade/remove`.\n- At root build time, `em.List()` enumerates that dir; for each extension it builds a Cobra subcommand with `DisableFlagParsing: true` and `RunE` calling `em.Dispatch(args, stdin, stdout, stderr)`. The `Dispatch` does the actual `exec.Cmd` with piped I/O (`manager.go:91`).\n- Conflict resolution is explicit: `cmd.Find([]string{name})` — if a built-in claims that verb, the extension is skipped (`root.go:197`).\n- Extensions go into `GroupID: \"extension\"` so they get their own section in help.\n- Disables auth check and telemetry per-extension (privacy: extension names may be sensitive). Also checks for extension updates async in PreRun/PostRun.\n- Shell scripts are supported on