{"parentUuid":"4158cf58-4245-4276-8a4b-2689c55aacce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DWkcGxHPfjR9M12FmBKZ7K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, easily. The migration path is clean because the two approaches share the same execution shape — both end in `exec.Cmd` with stdin/stdout/stderr piped through.\n\nWhat stays the same:\n- `entire-pgr` binary contract (no protocol, just argv + I/O passthrough)\n- Conflict rule (built-ins/agents win)\n- `DisableFlagParsing: true` on the dispatch path\n- `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` / cwd plumbing\n\nWhat changes when you go gh-style later:\n- **Source of truth** flips from PATH to a managed dir (e.g. `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/`). The `LookPath`/scan call gets replaced with a `manager.List()` over that dir.\n- **Registration** flips from lazy (resolve-on-unknown-arg) to eager (Cobra subcommands built at root construction). You add `cmd.AddCommand(...)` per plugin in a loop, mirroring `root.go:191-203`.\n- **New surface area**: `entire plugin install/list/upgrade/remove` commands. This is the bulk of the work — not the dispatch itself.\n\nTwo things worth getting right *now* so the later switch is trivial:\n\n1. **Put dispatch behind an interface.** Even if today's only impl is \"look up `entire-<name>` on PATH\", define something like `PluginResolver.Resolve(name) (path string, ok bool)` and `PluginRunner.Run(path, args, io)`. Later, `ManagedDirResolver` slots in alongside (or replaces) `PathResolver` without touching the Cobra wiring.\n2. **Don't leak \"PATH\" into user-visible naming.** Call them \"plugins\" or \"extensions\" in help/errors, not \"PATH plugins\". That way the docs don't need rewriting when the storage location changes.\n\nThe risk if you skip the abstraction: it's small. Even without it, the dispatch site is ~30 lines and easy to refactor. So don't over-engineer — a single `dispatchPlugin(name, args)` function is fine, and you can extract an interface when the second implementation arrives.\n\nOne thing that *would* be a breaking change for users: if today `entire pgr` resolves `entire-pgr` from PATH, and tomorrow it only resolves from `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/`, users who installed via Homebrew/apt will be surprised. gh sidesteps this by never having had PATH discovery. If you want both to coexist long-term, the resolver chain (managed dir → PATH fallback) handles it, but you'd want to decide that policy before users build muscle memory."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1824,"cache_read_input_tokens":103375,"output_tokens":871,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1824,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":103375,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1824},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CahRoBcE1kricu8Zdabb5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c06b7fd5-b817-4504-ae96-a9a2c56b1528","timestamp":"2026-05-04T11:12:20.493Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"705ab424-b185-46b1-96a4-0fb18926a1b1","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
