name))\n104\t\t}\n105\t\treturn name\n106\t}\n107\t\n108\t// runPlugin executes the resolved plugin binary, propagating its exit code.\n109\t// We deliberately use a context-free exec.Cmd so terminal signals propagate\n110\t// to the child via the process group rather than racing the parent's signal\n111\t// handler.\n112\tfunc runPlugin(ctx context.Context, binPath string, args []string, stdin io.Reader, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n113\t\tcmd := exec.Command(binPath, args...)\n114\t\tcmd.Stdin = stdin\n115\t\tcmd.Stdout = stdout\n116\t\tcmd.Stderr = stderr\n117\t\tcmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), \"ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION=\"+versioninfo.Version)\n118\t\tif repoRoot, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx); err == nil {\n119\t\t\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT=\"+repoRoot)\n120\t\t}\n121\t\n122\t\tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n123\t\t\tvar exitErr *exec.ExitError\n124\t\t\tif errors.As(err, &exitErr) {\n125\t\t\t\treturn exitErr.ExitCode()\n126\t\t\t}\n127\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, \"entire: failed to run plugin %s: %v\\n\", filepath.Base(binPath), err)\n128\t\t\treturn 1\n129\t\t}\n130\t\treturn 0\n131\t}"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ba5ab9df-7e3c-4df4-ab75-f125aa0d42aa","timestamp":"2026-05-04T11:28:01.083Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"705ab424-b185-46b1-96a4-0fb18926a1b1","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
