{"parentUuid":"3ea9893e-128d-40f8-80ce-c00185d9bcfd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01J5p9wH7Wv42ifz3XfQUGhU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Fully disabled.** No event at all — not even an anonymized \"an extension was used\" signal.\n\nThe implementation is annotation-based (`pkg/cmdutil/telemetry.go:50`):\n\n```go\nfunc DisableTelemetry(cmd *cobra.Command) {\n    cmd.Annotations[\"telemetry\"] = \"disabled\"\n}\n```\n\n`RecordTelemetry` checks that annotation first and returns early, so no `command_invocation` event is recorded. The wiring in `pkg/cmd/root/extension.go:87`:\n\n```go\nif !extensions.IsOfficial(ext.Name(), ext.Owner()) {\n    cmdutil.DisableTelemetry(cmd)\n}\n```\n\nTheir stated reasoning (comment in `extension.go:82-86`): extension names \"can be arbitrary (potentially including sensitive identifiers such as project or organization names)\" — so they don't even want the dimension carrying it.\n\n**The \"official\" allowlist is tiny and hardcoded** (`pkg/extensions/official.go:25`):\n\n```go\nvar OfficialExtensions = []OfficialExtension{\n    {Name: \"aw\", Owner: \"github\", Repo: \"gh-aw\"},\n    {Name: \"stack\", Owner: \"github\", Repo: \"gh-stack\"},\n}\n```\n\nTwo extensions, both owned by the `github` org, both checked owner-and-name (case-sensitive on name, case-insensitive on owner) — so a third-party `someuser/gh-stack` does *not* qualify even though the name matches. Only those two contribute their command path to telemetry.\n\n**For your case, three options:**\n\n1. **Match gh exactly** — fully disable telemetry for plugins. Simplest, most private. You lose visibility into plugin adoption.\n2. **Track presence only** — record a `plugin_invocation` event with no name/args, just the fact that *a* plugin ran. Tells you \"X% of users use plugins\" without leaking which one. Mid-privacy.\n3. **Allowlist** — like gh, hardcode a small set of known-safe plugin names (e.g. ones you ship yourself) that contribute their name to telemetry; everything else is silent.\n\nWhich one matches your appetite? Given you're following kubectl's structural model and gh's privacy posture is the strictest of the three, option 1 is the lowest-friction default. Option 3 makes sense if you plan to ship official Entire plugins yourself and want adoption metrics on them specifically."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1878,"cache_read_input_tokens":145755,"output_tokens":1370,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1370,"cache_read_input_tokens":145755,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1878},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CahTdRoTLdDpj7WcsbQVm","type":"assistant","uuid":"afb35206-778f-40e1-97d3-45fa9b51624b","timestamp":"2026-05-04T11:36:27.606Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"705ab424-b185-46b1-96a4-0fb18926a1b1","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
