{"parentUuid":"17ac5818-c6bd-4fe1-9a53-dba29fed2407","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HeE196hQ9ZhKPmA9w27wt8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three commits, reviewer's gap closed. The new integration tests:\n\n| Test | What it asserts about main.go's early dispatch |\n|---|---|\n| `HappyPath` | argv reaches plugin; stdout/stderr passthrough |\n| `ExitCodePropagation` | child's non-zero exit reaches parent's `os.Exit` |\n| `BuiltinWins` | dispatcher must defer to Cobra when name is built-in |\n| `PluginNotFound` | dispatcher falls through cleanly to Cobra's unknown-command error |\n| `FlagAfterPluginNameNotEatenByCobra` | confirms the dispatch happens *before* Cobra's flag parser sees `--help`/`--version` |\n| `StdinPassthrough` | parent stdin reaches child plugin |\n| `EnvVarsForwarded` | `ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION` is set in plugin env |\n| `AgentProtocolBinarySkipped` | `entire-agent-*` binaries are reserved (defense in depth at the binary level) |\n| `SigintReachesPlugin` *(Unix-only)* | parent's SIGINT handler → ctx cancel → `cmd.Cancel` → plugin trap fires; child cleans up rather than getting SIGKILL'd |\n\nThe signal test uses a readiness file (plugin writes `ready` after installing its trap, test waits for it before signalling) so the trap-install race is eliminated. Windows is left out of the signal coverage since the dispatcher's `cmd.Cancel = SIGINT` branch is Unix-only — on Windows the runtime falls back to `Process.Kill`, which is what gh, kubectl and the existing `external.Agent.run` also do."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1040,"cache_read_input_tokens":215057,"output_tokens":587,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1040,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tok